{"chunk_id": "ce9c0a185b92", "text": "This section captures the final verbal exchanges before the Kurukshetra war begins. Through Uluka, messenger of Duryodhana, the Pandava side delivers fierce responses and vows. Bhima swears to kill Dussasana and drink his blood and to break Duryodhana\u2019s thighs, recalling the humiliation of Draupadi. Other warriors also declare their targets: Sikhandin vows to bring down Bhishma, and Dhrishtadyumna promises to slay Drona. Yudhishthira alone speaks with restraint, regretting the coming slaughter while acknowledging that Duryodhana\u2019s obstinacy has made war inevitable. Uluka returns and reports everything, after which Duryodhana orders the Kaurava armies to be arrayed before sunrise. The scene then shifts to the Pandava camp, where Dhrishtadyumna organizes the army and assigns rival champions to face specific enemies, formally setting the stage for the epic battle.\nPandava allies send fierce vows through Uluka, and Dhrishtadyumna organizes the Pandava army\u2019s matchups for the impending Kurukshetra battle.\nThemes: pre-battle vows, vengeance, dharma vs adharma, war preparations, fate of warriors", "vector": [-0.004105956293642521, -0.021943865343928337, -0.015524262562394142, -0.00041442899964749813, -0.009874739684164524, 0.03342009708285332, -0.033774472773075104, -0.002918465994298458, -0.012743798084557056, -0.028022725135087967, 0.021194230765104294, 0.01422943826764822, 0.005428039934486151, 0.012287202291190624, 0.011803346686065197, 0.009240956977009773, 0.03232971951365471, -0.002947429195046425, 0.027136793360114098, -0.020103851333260536, -0.000243631424382329, -0.017514202743768692, 0.004654552787542343, 0.027532055974006653, -0.022352756932377815, 0.03159371390938759, -0.0037992873694747686, -0.01812754198908806, 0.003175727091729641, 0.001084415358491242, -0.02856791391968727, -0.011387639679014683, 0.008913843892514706, -0.006760346237570047, -0.030012665316462517, 0.00806879997253418, 0.0007458017789758